-14T14:12:16Z","closed_at":"2026-05-14T14:12:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6-stable\nNot present earlier\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable.double (223b3f9e1) - Steam Runtime 2 (soldier) 2 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (nvidia) - AMD Ryzen 9 3900 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 31.24 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThis is a regression in behavior caused by binding handle commits to final mouse position differences. Documentation is non-existent for the `_begin_handle_action` method, however it seems to be a general expectation that commits are always called after a begin action, especially when the mouse is not actually moved. A \"begin\" is always followed by an \"end.\" This \"end\" may be to clean up state which affects gizmo rendering/ interactions for developer plugins.\n\nAdditionally, it is a poor assumption that NO change should be made if the mouse moves and happens to return exactly to the original location, such as a tool that requires dragging over various objects with the mouse button held, and then released. It is possible to drop the action entirely if the dev happened to return to the original location. This often results in bad state when clicking handles and returning to the original location.\n\nThe following commit causes this regression:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/060f9b7a16b3a169d67af33b266e8c1284afbc8b\n\nIn my opinion, this should just be reverted entirely and implement a better system that waits until mouse motion before starting the edit, instead of effectively dropping the edit action at the end. Otherwise, expose this method (`can_commit_handle_on_click()`) as new API and set the default to be TRUE, and fix the spam directly on the gizmo plugins that require mouse motion for action commits.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNo steps to reproduce, the change is clear from the couple lines of code in the commit which alters default behavior for others with NO remedy made available.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115734/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}